@startuml
title Option C - Event-Centred CQRS and Saga Deployment Diagram (Requirement 6)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

node "Client Device" as Client {
  artifact "Browser / Postman" as Browser
}
node "Distributed Container Environment\n(example: Docker Compose)" as Host {
  node "api-gateway" as Gateway
  node "booking-command-saga" as Command
  node "availability-query-projector" as Query
  node "payment-worker" as Payment
  node "notification-worker" as Notify
  queue "event-broker\nRabbitMQ" as Broker
  database "booking-write-db" as WriteDB
  database "availability-read-db" as ReadDB
  database "payment-db" as PayDB
  database "notification-db" as NotifyDB
}

Browser --> Gateway : HTTP commands / queries
Gateway --> Command : reservation command
Gateway --> Query : availability query
Command --> WriteDB : SQL; hold / confirm / atomic overlap check
Command --> Broker : publish events
Broker --> Payment : PaymentRequested
Payment --> PayDB : simulated result
Payment --> Broker : PaymentSucceeded / Failed
Broker --> Command : continue saga
Broker --> Query : confirmed / cancelled events
Query --> ReadDB : update / read projection
Broker --> Notify : notification event
Notify --> NotifyDB : delivery record
@enduml
